<title>UK: Newman Tonks spurns FKI offer.</title>
<headline>Newman Tonks spurns FKI offer.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Building supplier Newman Tonks Plc on Tuesday said rejected a hostile bid for it from engineering group FKI Plc, saying the 195.7 million pound offer was &quot;opportunistic&quot; and undervalued Newman's business.</p>
<p>The company recommended that shareholders reject the offer and take no immediate action.</p>
<p>Newman Tonks said the bid did not reflect its value of its brands, market position or its future prospects.</p>
</text>
